@startuml Expiry Process

title Auto-Expiry Process - Direct Database Operation

start

:Application Startup;

:Mark Expired Trades\n(Synchronous);

fork
  :Handle API Requests;
  
  while (Request Received?) is (yes)
    if (Write Operation?) then (yes)
      :POST/PUT/DELETE Trade;
      :Queue to Kafka (202);
      note right
        Write operations are
        async via Kafka
      end note
    elseif (Read Operation?) then (yes)
      :GET Trade(s);
      :Query Database (200);
      note right
        Read operations are
        sync from DB
      end note
    else (Expiry Trigger)
      :POST /trades/expire;
      :Check All Trades;
      :Mark Expired Trades;
      :Return Count;
      note right
        Expiry is synchronous
        (not via Kafka)
      end note
    endif
  endwhile (no)
  
fork again
  :Scheduled Expiry Check\n(if implemented);
  
  :Cron Job / Scheduler;
  :Mark Expired Trades;
  :Update Database Directly;
  
end fork

:Continue Operations;

stop

note right
  **Expiry Conditions:**
  - maturity_date < today
  - expired = False
  
  **Action:**
  Set expired = True
  
  **Note:**
  Expiry is a read-modify-write
  operation done synchronously,
  not through Kafka queue
end note

note left
  **Architecture:**
  
  Write Path (Async):
  CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE → Kafka
  
  Read Path (Sync):
  GET → Database
  
  Expiry (Sync):
  POST /trades/expire → Database
end note

@enduml
